<p class=3D"MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-41w77t"><em>[options=
]</em> would be things like -p to map ports, -v to map volumes, and -d to d=
aemonize.</p>
<p class=3D"MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-41w77t"><code class=
=3D"MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-inline-code css-1r5tc1u">docker-openre=
sty</code> symlinks <code class=3D"MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-inline-=
code css-1r5tc1u">/usr/local/openresty/nginx/logs/access.log</code> and <co=
de class=3D"MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-inline-code css-1r5tc1u">error=
.log</code> to <code class=3D"MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-inline-code =
css-1r5tc1u">/dev/stdout</code> and <code class=3D"MuiTypography-root MuiTy=
pography-inline-code css-1r5tc1u">/dev/stderr</code> respectively, so that =
Docker logging works correctly.  If you change the log paths in your <code =
class=3D"MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-inline-code css-1r5tc1u">nginx.co=
nf</code>, you should symlink those paths as well. This is not possible wit=
h the <code class=3D"MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-inline-code css-1r5tc=
1u">windows</code> image.</p>
<p class=3D"MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-41w77t">Temporary di=
rectories such as <code class=3D"MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-inline-co=
de css-1r5tc1u">client_body_temp_path</code> are stored in <code class=3D"M=
uiTypography-root MuiTypography-inline-code css-1r5tc1u">/var/run/openresty=
/</code>.  You may consider mounting that volume, rather than writing to a =
container-local directory.  This is not done for <code class=3D"MuiTypograp=
hy-root MuiTypography-inline-code css-1r5tc1u">windows</code>.</p>
